:"(1\/2vol) Σᵢⱼ dᵢ dⱼ R(i, j) (commute times are vol · R), with L_g the Laplacian grounded at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the vertex of largest degree and eliminated as for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numberOfSpanningTrees"},{"text":". Every term is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sum of positive ones and the difference loses at most a factor n, so the result keeps its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"title":"Edges","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/kemenyConstant(weight:)-4bx2c":{"title":"kemenyConstant(weight:)","abstract":[{"text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","ty